cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use MCPSync in your work or research, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: MCPSync
abstract: >-
  MCPSync is a CLI tool that synchronizes Model Context Protocol (MCP) server
  configurations across multiple AI coding agents (Claude Desktop, Claude Code,
  Cursor, VS Code, Windsurf, Gemini CLI, GitHub Copilot, OpenAI Codex CLI, Zed,
  Continue, and more) in a single command. It auto-discovers agent configs,
  merges them into one deduplicated list, and writes back to all agents with
  atomic writes and automatic backups.
